      "category": "cooling",
      "title": "EA888 2.0 TFSI coolant leak from water pump / thermostat housing",
      "description": "The SQ2's EA888 2.0 TFSI shares the well-documented Volkswagen-Group composite water pump / thermostat housing assembly that develops slow coolant leaks. The plastic housing and the shaft seal on the electrically-controlled thermostat unit are a known wear point that typically starts as a slow coolant loss (often with no obvious puddle because seepage evaporates off hot surfaces). Left unaddressed it can lead to low coolant, overheating risk and temperature warnings. This is one of the most common EA888 Gen3 platform faults across Audi/VW and applies to the SQ2's engine.",
      "solution": "Replace the failed water pump / thermostat housing assembly, ideally with the latest revised, more heat-resistant unit; many shops fit an upgraded repair kit and a new gasket. Catch it early by watching for slowly dropping coolant level and a faint sweet smell. Combine with a coolant flush and refill.",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "symptoms": [
        "Slowly dropping coolant level",
        "Sweet coolant smell",
        "Low coolant warning",
        "Coolant residue around water pump/thermostat housing",
        "Occasional engine temperature fluctuation"
      ],
