      "title": "Internal fuse box wiring harness can work loose, causing sudden loss of drive (Recall 97HO)",
      "description": "Audi issued a safety recall (campaign 97HO, also linked to the fuse-carrier electrical-connector recall covering vehicles built roughly Oct 2020–May 2023) because the internal fuse box wiring harness / power-supply connector to the fuse carrier may not have been correctly installed and can come loose. If the connection fails, the consequences are serious: the instrument cluster may fail to illuminate, exterior lamps may switch off, and the vehicle can suffer a sudden loss of motive power while driving. This is the single most safety-critical documented fault for the SQ2/Q2 and was the subject of formal EU/UK recall action.",
      "solution": "This is a manufacturer recall — affected cars should be taken to an Audi dealer to have the fuse box wiring harness/connector inspected and correctly secured or replaced free of charge. Owners can check eligibility by VIN via the Audi recall checker or the DVSA recall database. Do not ignore intermittent dash, lighting, or power warnings on affected build years.",
