      "title": "PCV / crankcase ventilation valve diaphragm failure causing rough idle and lean-running codes",
      "description": "The EA888 2.0 TFSI uses an integrated PCV (crankcase ventilation) valve in the valve cover whose rubber diaphragm and check valve are a known failure point across the engine family. When the diaphragm tears, the seal is lost and unmetered air enters, producing rough idle, possible whistling/screeching from the engine bay, a lean-running condition and sometimes increased oil consumption. It is a recurring, inexpensive-to-diagnose VW-Group fault that affects the SQ2's engine.",
      "solution": "Replace the PCV valve (or the valve-cover assembly that integrates it) with the latest revised part; some owners fit a catch-can to reduce recurrence. A quick field test — briefly covering the bleeder hole on the cap to see if idle stabilises or whistling stops — helps confirm before replacement.",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": "high",
